Based on the search results, here's what I found about the Xiaomi MiMo token plan and the mimo-v2.5-asr API audio transcription request format:

## API Request Format

The mimo-v2.5-asr API uses a chat completions format where audio is passed as a Base64-encoded string with the data type "input_audio". The basic request structure is:

```python
completion = client.chat.completions.create(
    model="mimo-v2.5-asr",
    messages=[
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": [
                {
                    "type": "input_audio",
                    "input_audio": {
                        "data": f"data:audio/wav;base64,{audio_base64}"
                    }
                }
            ]
        }
    ],
    extra_body={
        "asr_options": {
            "language": "auto"
        }
    },
    stream=True
)
```

## Audio Format Requirements

Only wav and mp3 audio sample files are supported, and before passing audio to the API, convert the file to a Base64 encoded string, with the encoded string size not exceeding 10 MB.

## Language Options

Set asr_options.language to specify the language, with auto detection used if not configured. Manual specification is recommended when the language is confirmed to improve recognition performance. Supported values are: auto, zh, en.

## Token Plan Setup

Create a pay-as-you-go key in the Xiaomi MiMo console, or open your Token Plan subscription page and copy the regional OpenAI-compatible base URL plus the matching tp-... key.


